  "method_notes": [
    "challenge_v2 was written by a separate assistant without access to the detector or to challenge_v1, and was evaluated exactly once per build after all changes were final. No rule, threshold or list was adjusted after seeing it.",
    "Design decisions for embedded checks (common domain endings for bare addresses; links raise a message only at Elevated/High) were made on the historical train/validation split, not on any test data.",
    "The OpenPhish feed is time-varying and was disabled for this evaluation so results are reproducible.",
    "Re-evaluated once after fixes from an independent code review (phishing-feed host matching, retry cooldown, link/number extraction); these fixes were not informed by challenge_v2."
  ],
